It is lunch time now.
I go outside the office.
Here the street is very busy.
People are walking here and there.
A tourist comes near me.
There is a mobile in his hand.
He looks at a map there.
He asks me politely.
"Madam, where is the large post office here?"
I know its location well.
I show him the way.
I say.
"Sir, you go forward on this road."
"From there, you go to the left side."
"The large post office is right there."
The tourist smiles.
He says, "Thank you, madam."
I say, "Welcome."
He walks forward.
